  "content": "PM Karki chooses new social media accounts over Oli’s\nOnlinekhabar\nMonday, October 6, 2025\n0\nComments\nFile\nKathmandu, October 6\nTraditionally, when a prime minister leaves office, the official social media usernames and passwords are handed over to the incoming prime minister, who continues to use the same accounts as they represent the government.\nHowever, Sushila Karki, who rose to power with support from the Gen Z youth movement, has decided not to use the social media accounts previously operated by former Prime Minister KP Sharma Oli. Instead, she has chosen to operate new accounts on Facebook, X (Twitter), and Instagram.\nAccording to a press release issued by Rabi Lal Panth, joint secretary and spokesperson at the Office of the Prime Minister and Council of Ministers, the accounts being used by the current prime minister have different usernames from those used by her predecessors.\nWhile former prime ministers used the X handle @PM_nepal, Prime Minister Karki will now use the handle @pmsushilakarki, the release stated.\nWhy the change?\nOfficials at the Prime Minister’s Office explained that Karki herself expressed a preference not to use the old accounts, leading to the creation of new ones. “The prime minister said she would not operate the old accounts and wanted new ones, so they were set up accordingly,” a source said.\nAjayabhadra Khanal, chief advisor to Prime Minister Karki, added that since the old accounts still displayed former Prime Minister Oli’s past activities, it was more appropriate to start afresh. “We decided to use new accounts. When a new government comes, we will also hand them over,” Khanal told Onlinekhabar.\nOli’s secretariat only handed over the X account, and that too just this past Sunday, Khanal said. The Facebook and Instagram accounts have not been transferred, which is why new accounts were created.\nCurrently, both the old @PM_nepal and the new @pmsushilakarki X accounts are accessible to Karki’s secretariat, though most updates are being made from the latter. Official government announcements posted on @pmsushilakarki are sometimes retweeted from @PM_nepal, he added.\nDiscussions are ongoing with technical teams regarding the management of the new Facebook and Instagram accounts.\nReact to this post\nHot Topics\nElection Commission\nlichhibari land scam\nConversation\nNew\nOld\nPopular\nAdd Comment\nLogin to comment\nRemenber me\nForgot password?\nLogin\nNot have account yet?\nSignup Now\nOr use Social Media?\nGoogle\nFacebook\nTwitter\nForgot Password?\nSend Password Reset Link\nBack\nRelated News\nBanning the Social Media: Why Nepal’s blanket social media ban misses the mark\n1 month ago\nUnregistered social media to be gradually blocked from today, Minister Gurung says\n1 month ago\nHow social media influencers could create modern gods and goddesses?\n1 year ago\nMan arrested for abuse through social media\n2 years ago\nTikTok in commitment letter to Nepal, says ready to follow Nepal’s laws\n2 years ago\nGovt approves guideline mandating use of social media, including TikTok, by public offices\n2 years ago\nMost Read\nHighways blocked nationwide as heavy rainfall disrupts travel\nNepalis celebrate Bijaya Dashami, auspicious Tika time set at 11:53 am\nMonsoon triggers flood and landslide risks in several districts, DHM issues special alert\nFlood risks in Kathmandu, KMC launches helpline service\nCAA publishes domestic airfare rates, Kathmandu–Dhangadhi at Rs 17,579\nSubscribe to our newsletter\nSubscribe to Onlinekhabar English to get notified of exclusive news stories.\nEditor's Pick\nEditor's Pick\n4 government buildings, including Supreme Court, declared unfit for use\n3 weeks ago\nEditor's Pick\nCharred body found at Koteshwor Bhatbhateni, Gen-Z protest death toll rises to 74\n3 weeks ago\nEditor's Pick\nNo consensus on Hami Nepal’s claim of leading the Gen-Z movement\n3 weeks ago\nEditor's Pick\nDecades-old irrigation projects stall as Madhesh faces drought, food crisis looms\n3 months ago\nEditor's Pick\nNepal’s farming crisis: When plans stay on paper and fields suffer\n3 months ago\nAlso Read\nPolitics\nElection Commission invites parties for talks on upcoming House election\n8 hours ago\nSociety\nSeven charged in Pokhara Lichhibari land scam involving former ministers and officials\n8 hours ago\nOpinion\nWhen a joke fuels division: Casual hate speech and the Gen Z revolution in Nepal\n15 hours ago\nBlog\nWhen Nepal’s youth dared to dream of a better tomorrow\n1 day ago\nSociety\nAI and fake accounts drove one third of online buzz during Nepal Gen Z uprising\n2 days ago",
